    {
      "title": "Singleton as Global State",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Singleton as Global State",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a singleton is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Private constructor== + static `getInstance()`",
                "One instance per ==JVM== (per class loader)",
                "Gives a **global access point**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class Config {",
                "  private static final Config INSTANCE = new Config();",
                "  private Config() {}",
                "  static Config getInstance() { return INSTANCE; }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why it is global state",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "What goes wrong"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:Hidden dependency}",
                  "`Config.getInstance()` inside methods; the signature does not show the need"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Shared mutable state}",
                  "Anyone can change it: order-dependent bugs, action at a distance, thread races"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Breaks SRP}",
                  "Manages its own lifecycle and does business work"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Tight coupling}",
                  "Every caller is bound to the concrete class"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Better: inject one instance",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Composition root",
                    "sub": "new Config() once",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Constructor",
                    "sub": "passed in",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Callers",
                    "sub": "depend on it openly",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Checkout(Config config) { this.config = config; }",
                "// at startup:",
                "Config config = new Config();",
                "new Checkout(config);"
              ],
              "note": "the constructor now reveals what Checkout needs"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==Single instance== is a **lifetime choice**, not a global access point. Create it once at the root and pass it in."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
