    {
      "title": "Testing Problems with Singletons",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Testing Problems with Singletons",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. How singletons break tests",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "Cause and effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "State leaks",
                  "State lives for the whole JVM; test A breaks test B, so ==order== matters"
                ],
                [
                  "No mock",
                  "`getInstance()` is hard-wired; stubbing DB, clock or mailer needs PowerMock or reflection"
                ],
                [
                  "Parallel runs",
                  "Shared mutable state makes them ==flaky== and non-deterministic"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Workarounds are smells",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`reset()` or `setInstance()` only for tests weakens the design",
                "Fix: extract an ==interface==, inject it via the constructor"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "// hard-wired: cannot fake it",
                "void pay() { Mailer.getInstance().send(); }",
                "// injected: pass a fake in tests",
                "Checkout(Mailer mailer) { this.mailer = mailer; }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Testable design",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Interface",
                    "sub": "code depends on it",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fake",
                    "sub": "injected in tests",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Real instance",
                    "sub": "wired once at startup",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Spring singleton",
              "text": "One bean per ==container==, not a global; it is injected."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is a singleton hard to test?** Hidden global state leaks between tests and cannot be mocked.",
                "**Why avoid reset() for tests?** It is a test-only back door; inject an interface instead."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
